<LanguageData>
  <!-- General -->
  <SocialInteractions_SettingsCategory>Social Interactions</SocialInteractions_SettingsCategory>
  <SocialInteractions_SettingsTitle>Social Interactions Settings</SocialInteractions_SettingsTitle>
  <SocialInteractions_SettingsDesc>If enabled, pawns will stop their current activities during social interactions.</SocialInteractions_SettingsDesc>
  
  <!-- Feature Toggle Labels -->
  <SocialInteractions_PawnsStopOnInteraction>Pawns stop on interaction</SocialInteractions_PawnsStopOnInteraction>
  <SocialInteractions_PawnsStopOnInteractionDesc>If enabled, pawns will stop their current activities during social interactions.</SocialInteractions_PawnsStopOnInteractionDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableCombatTaunts>Enable Combat Taunts</SocialInteractions_EnableCombatTaunts>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableCombatTauntsDesc>If enabled, pawns will taunt each other in combat.</SocialInteractions_EnableCombatTauntsDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableDrama>Drama Interactions</SocialInteractions_EnableDrama>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableDramaDesc>If enabled, pawns may engage in drama-causing interactions like badmouthing.</SocialInteractions_EnableDramaDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableDatingFeature>Enable Dating Feature</SocialInteractions_EnableDatingFeature>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableDatingFeatureDesc>If enabled, pawns will be able to go on dates.</SocialInteractions_EnableDatingFeatureDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_OpenChatLogWindow>Open Chat Log Window</SocialInteractions_OpenChatLogWindow>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableLLMInteractions>Enable LLM Interactions</SocialInteractions_EnableLLMInteractions>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableLLMInteractionsDesc>If enabled, Deep Talk interactions will use the configured LLM API.</SocialInteractions_EnableLLMInteractionsDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableInteractiveNegotiation>Enable Interactive Negotiation</SocialInteractions_EnableInteractiveNegotiation>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableInteractiveNegotiationDesc>If enabled, negotiations will take place in a dedicated window with choices. If disabled, they will happen via speech bubbles in the main view.</SocialInteractions_EnableInteractiveNegotiationDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_PreventSpam>Prevent Spam</SocialInteractions_PreventSpam>
  <SocialInteractions_PreventSpamDesc>If enabled, new LLM interactions will not start until the previous one has finished displaying its speech bubbles.</SocialInteractions_PreventSpamDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_UseTextBackground>Use Text Background</SocialInteractions_UseTextBackground>
  <SocialInteractions_UseTextBackgroundDesc>If enabled, LLM-generated text will be displayed with a background instead of a drop shadow.</SocialInteractions_UseTextBackgroundDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableVerboseLogging>Enable Verbose Logging</SocialInteractions_EnableVerboseLogging>
  <SocialInteractions_EnableVerboseLoggingDesc>If enabled, detailed logs will be written to the Player.log file for debugging purposes.</SocialInteractions_EnableVerboseLoggingDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_ShowDefaultBubbles>Show Interaction Bubbles (Default)</SocialInteractions_ShowDefaultBubbles>
  <SocialInteractions_ShowDefaultBubblesDesc>If enabled, standard interaction bubbles and fallback summaries will be displayed above pawns.</SocialInteractions_ShowDefaultBubblesDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_ShowLlmBubbles>Show Dialogue Bubbles (LLM)</SocialInteractions_ShowLlmBubbles>
  <SocialInteractions_ShowLlmBubblesDesc>If enabled, LLM-generated dialogue lines will be displayed above pawns. If disabled, they will be hidden, but TTS and chat logs will still work.</SocialInteractions_ShowLlmBubblesDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_ForceChatCompletion>Force Chat Completion</SocialInteractions_ForceChatCompletion>
  <SocialInteractions_ForceChatCompletionDesc>If enabled, KoboldCpp, LM Studio, and Ollama will use OpenAI-compatible chat completion endpoints instead of text completion. This is recommended for newer models.</SocialInteractions_ForceChatCompletionDesc>
  <SocialInteractions_DisableLlmThinking>Disable Reasoning (Thoughts)</SocialInteractions_DisableLlmThinking>
  <SocialInteractions_DisableLlmThinkingDesc>If enabled, tries to minimize or disable internal reasoning/thinking for models that support it (Gemini 2+, Claude 3.7+, Deepseek R1). This saves output tokens and makes responses significantly faster.</SocialInteractions_DisableLlmThinkingDesc>
  
